# Dev workflow

## Build / test

```bash
./gradlew :core:test :demo:build
```

Windows: `.\gradlew.bat …`. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs the same on Ubuntu + JDK 17 Temurin.

## Demo CLI (`:demo`)

```bash
# Mock transcript → JSON report
./gradlew :demo:run --args="--transcript samples/transcripts/bank_scam_01.txt --output report.json"

# Eval suite
./gradlew :demo:run --args="--eval --output reports/eval.json"

# ML component status
./gradlew :demo:run --args="--status"
```

## Local setup (Windows)

- JDK: `scripts/setup-jdk.ps1` → project-local `.jdk/` (used by `gradlew.bat`)
- Models (gitignored): `scripts/setup-models.ps1` → `models/` + `core/libs/` (Sherpa JARs)
  - Silero VAD, MiniLM ONNX, Sherpa-ONNX GigaAM v2 Russian STT
  - Override root: env `SCAMDEFENDER_MODELS`
- Without models: keyword/heuristic fallbacks still work for transcript demos

## Do not commit

`.jdk/`, `models/**` binaries, `core/libs/`, `reports/`, `report.json`, secrets (see `.gitignore`).

## Android

`android-app/` is a stub; enable only with Android SDK + uncomment `include(":android-app")` and restore Android plugins. Not part of default MVP loop.
